{title: O Sing a Song of Bethlehem}
{key: Am}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [Am]sing a [Em]song of [C]Bethle[G]hem, of [C]shepherds [F]watching [G]there[**]
And [F]of the [G]news that [C]came to [G]them from [C]angels [Dm]in the [Am]air.[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [Em]light that [C]shone on [G]Bethle[C]hem [**]fills all the [F]world to[G]day[**]
Of [F]Jesus' [Dm]birth and [D]peace on [G]earth the [C]angels [F]sing al[Am]way[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [Am]sing a [Em]song of [C]Naza[G]reth, of [C]sunny [F]days of [G]joy[**]
O [F]sing of [G]fragrant [C]flowers' [G]breath, and [C]of the [Dm]sinless [Am]Boy[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
For [Em]now the [C]flowers of [G]Naz[C]areth [**]in every [F]heart may [G]grow[**]
Now [F]spreads the [Dm]fame of [D]his dear [G]name on [C]all the [F]winds that [Am]blow[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 5}
O [Am]sing a [Em]song of [C]Gali[G]lee, of [C]lake and [F]woods and [G]hill[**]
Of [F]him who [G]walked u[C]pon the [G]sea and [C]bade the [Dm]waves be [Am]still[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 6}
For [Em]though like [C]waves on [G]Gali[C]lee, [**]dark seas of [F]trouble [G]roll[**]
When [F]faith has [Dm]heard the [D]Master's [G]work, falls [C]peace u[F]pon the [Am]soul[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 7}
O [Am]sing a [Em]song of [C]Calva[G]ry, its [C]glory [F]and dis[G]may[**]
Of [F]him who [G]hung u[C]pon the [G]tree, and [C]took our [Dm]sins a[Am]way.[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 8}
For [Em]he who [C]died on [G]Calva[C]ry [**]is risen [F]from the [G]grave[**]
And [F]Christ, our [Dm]Lord, by [D]heaven a[G]dored, is [C]mighty [F]now to [Am]save[**].
{end_of_verse}
